what = IntroWhat(
  "Steps tell users what to click; concepts tell them why. This topic covers why understanding matters (mental models and transfer), techniques for explaining (analogies, worked examples, refutation, diagrams), interactive explanations (simulators, what-ifs, Predict → Observe → Explain), and findings from learning science that make understanding stick.",
  "Teaching concepts in software docs means helping users build a correct mental model of how the product works, so they can act correctly even when the manual's steps don't cover their situation.",
  [
    "Procedural vs conceptual knowledge, transfer, and Don Norman's three models",
    "Analogy with limits, concrete before abstract, refutation, non-examples, dual coding, cognitive load",
    "Explorable explanations, concept simulators, clickable flows, what-if scenarios, POE",
    "Retrieval practice, spacing, self-explanation and explanatory feedback",
  ],
  ["documentation", "instructional-design", "mental-models", "learning-science", "explanation"],
)

why = IntroWhy(
  "No manual can document every situation. Users who understand the idea handle the undocumented cases; users who only know the clicks guess.",
  "Docs that teach only steps create the Hollow Clicker: users who follow the manual perfectly, then archive confidential data thinking it's deleted, or give a contractor access to every project.",
)
